    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1327">

                <pb facs="1199" n="941" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg941"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.6311/156</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in Austria-Hungary</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Penfield</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-22T21:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 22, 1915, 9 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>910. To-day Doctor Dumba informs Department leave of absence granted him
                    officially by his Government. He requests safe-conduct for himself and Madame
                    Dumba on steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Rotterdam</hi>, sailing September 28.
                    Department has replied that it is still await a definite reply from Vienna to
                    its note of September 8, requesting his recall. Urge an immediate reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
